          "text": "The pattern indexes uniquely as primitive tetragonal with \\(a \\approx 3.3244\\) \u00c5 and \\(c \\approx 3.0726\\) \u00c5. The strong/weak intensity alternation is consistent with a CsCl-like ordered Mg/Ni framework. Hydrogen occupies the in-plane \\(2e\\) site, producing square-planar NiH\\(_4\\) coordination and NiH\\(_2\\) sheets.\n\n```cif\ndata_MgNiH2\n_audit_creation_method              'Structure solution from Cu Kalpha1 powder XRD'\n_chemical_name_common               'magnesium nickel dihydride'\n_chemical_formula_structural         'MgNiH2'\n_chemical_formula_sum                'H2 Mg Ni'\n_chemical_formula_weight             85.014\n_cell_formula_units_Z                1\n\n_cell_length_a                       3.3244\n_cell_length_b                       3.3244\n_cell_length_c                       3.0726\n_cell_angle_alpha                    90\n_cell_angle_beta                     90\n_cell_angle_gamma                    90\n_cell_volume                         33.957\n\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt            'P 4/m m m'\n_space_group_IT_number               123\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type               'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength         1.5406\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_Wyckoff_symbol\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\nNi1  Ni  1  a  0.000000  0.000000  0.000000  1.0\nMg1  Mg  1  d  0.500000  0.500000  0.500000  1.0\nH1   H   2  e  0.000000  0.500000  0.000000  1.0\n```\n\n### Principal indexing\n\n| Observed 2\u03b8 (\u00b0) | hkl |\n|---:|:---:|\n| 26.79 | 100 |\n| 29.04 | 001 |\n| 38.26 | 110 |\n| 39.92 | 101 |\n| 48.73 | 111 |\n| 55.22 | 200 |\n| 60.19 | 002 |\n| 62.41 | 210 |\n| 63.60 | 201 |\n| 67.05 | 102 |\n| 70.28 | 211 |\n| 73.60 | 112 |\n| 81.90 | 220 |\n| 86.12 | 202 |\n| 89.12 | 221 |\n\nAn origin-shifted but identical CIF can place Mg at \\(1a\\), Ni at \\(1d\\), and H at \\(2f\\). This is 